  "lessons": [
    "The canonical report path is working: restored single-core IPC/UIPC rises from 0.212457 to 0.853065 on the same checkpoint lineage.",
    "The earlier 4-core MESI timing run used a mismatched 1 MB shared L2 target even though the source-side 4-core experiment was warmed with an effective 4 MB shared cache. Correcting gem5 to 4 MB raises aggregate IPC/UIPC from 0.796744 to 0.839293.",
    "After the 4 MB correction, branch and TLB counters remain clean, while load-to-use latency and rescheduled-load counts still indicate substantial shared lower-level service delay in the 4-core run.",
    "The remaining 4-core gap is therefore no longer explained by TLB misses, BTB/TAGE failure, or the old 1 MB LLC mismatch alone."
